| ID | Functional Requirement | Proposed Priority |
|---|---|---|
| FR-01 | The system shall allow users to record the completion of selected health habits, including nutrition, physical activity and goal-progress tracking. | Must-have |
| FR-02 | The system shall allow users to view their recorded habit history and progress over time. | Must-have |
| FR-03 | The system shall allow users to edit or delete submitted habit logs, with confirmation before deletion. | Must-have |
| FR-04 | The system shall recalculate affected streaks, milestones and XP rewards when habit logs are edited or deleted, according to approved business rules. | Must-have |
| FR-05 | The system shall track consecutive days of habit completion and display the user's active streak. | Must-have |
| FR-06 | The system shall allow users to temporarily pause an active streak for a predefined period without losing the preserved streak. | Proposed |
| FR-07 | The system shall provide a predefined grace period for eligible missed days, according to approved rules. | Proposed |
| FR-08 | The system shall track and display milestones achieved through defined habit-related activities. | Must-have |
| FR-09 | The system shall send habit reminders according to user-configured preferences and supported notification settings. | Proposed |
| FR-10 | The system shall award and display non-monetary XP rewards for eligible activities according to defined reward rules. | Proposed |

Priorities are provisional and must be confirmed during scope approval.

## 7.3 Acceptance Criteria

Acceptance criteria define the conditions that must be met to demonstrate that a requirement has been satisfied. They may be documented with the requirements or elaborated later in functional specifications and user stories.

Examples include:

- Users can record a habit and subsequently view the recorded entry.
- The system requests confirmation before deleting a habit log.
- Editing or deleting a log causes affected streaks, milestones and rewards to be recalculated according to approved rules.
- A streak pause preserves the streak for the configured duration.
- A grace period operates according to approved eligibility and missed-day rules.
- XP is awarded only when the approved reward conditions are met.
- Reminders respect the user's configured preferences and supported notification settings.

## 7.4 Rules Requiring Further Definition

The following business rules remain open:

- Maximum streak-pause duration and eligibility.
- Grace-period duration and eligible missed days.
- Milestone thresholds and completion rules.
- XP eligibility and reward recalculation.
- Whether XP already awarded is retained or reversed after log deletion.
- Reminder frequency, timing and user preferences.
- Data retention and deletion behavior.

These rules must be validated with relevant stakeholders before the requirements are baselined.

