## 7.3 Acceptance Criteria

Acceptance criteria define the conditions that must be met to demonstrate that a requirement has been satisfied. They may be documented with the requirements or elaborated later in functional specifications and user stories.

Examples include:

- Users can record a habit and subsequently view the recorded entry.
- The system requests confirmation before deleting a habit log.
- Editing or deleting a log causes affected streaks, milestones and rewards to be recalculated according to approved rules.
- A streak pause preserves the streak for the configured duration.
- A grace period operates according to approved eligibility and missed-day rules.
- XP is awarded only when the approved reward conditions are met.
- Reminders respect the user's configured preferences and supported notification settings.

## 7.4 Rules Requiring Further Definition

The following business rules remain open:

- Maximum streak-pause duration and eligibility.
- Grace-period duration and eligible missed days.
- Milestone thresholds and completion rules.
- XP eligibility and reward recalculation.
- Whether XP already awarded is retained or reversed after log deletion.
- Reminder frequency, timing and user preferences.
- Data retention and deletion behavior.

These rules must be validated with relevant stakeholders before the requirements are baselined.

