# 12. Success Criteria

## 12.1 Primary Success Metric

**Free-to-paid subscription conversion rate** is the primary business success metric.

The baseline, target improvement, eligible user population and measurement window must be agreed with Growth/Product and Analytics before the experiment begins.

The project must not assume a numerical target without sufficient evidence and stakeholder approval.

## 12.2 Supporting Metrics

| Metric Category | Evaluation Purpose |
|---|---|
| Engagement | Determine whether users demonstrate sustained meaningful habit-related activity beyond initial onboarding. |
| Retention | Evaluate whether users continue using the application over agreed measurement windows, including Day-30 retention where appropriate. |
| User Experience | Monitor usability feedback, complaints and signs of unwanted pressure or frustration. |
| Financial Viability | Compare implementation and recurring costs with expected commercial value. |
| Technical Quality | Verify that approved performance, reliability, security and usability requirements are met. |

## 12.3 Evaluation Rules

- Compare experiment outcomes against validated baselines and predefined success thresholds.
- Evaluate statistical and practical significance using an appropriate experiment design, sample size and observation period.
- Monitor guardrail metrics to identify unacceptable effects on retention, user experience, technical quality or cost.
- Evaluate whether observed outcomes differ across relevant user segments.
- Use the findings to determine whether to iterate, expand or discontinue the intervention.
- Treat positive pilot results as evidence for further evaluation, not automatic approval for a full rollout.

## 12.4 Decision-Making

A successful outcome requires more than achieving a conversion target. The business must also consider the quality of evidence, user experience, technical feasibility, costs and sustainability.

Final success thresholds, experiment duration, rollout criteria and decision authority must be approved by the appropriate business sponsor and stakeholders.

